# Accepted gaps for 64-array-dispatch. Each line is an edge the TypeScript compiler
# resolves and this engine does not. A NEW missing edge fails the suite;
# a line here that STARTS working also fails, so the debt cannot rot.
#
# All three are the same family: a callable registered as DATA and reached through
# the collection holding it, rather than named at the call site. They are pinned
# here rather than left silent because an absent edge and an unmodelled one are
# indistinguishable to a consumer, and an empty impact answer reads as "nothing
# depends on this", which is the most costly thing to say incorrectly.
#
# Measured against the TypeScript compiler's own answer (checker.getResolvedSignature,
# via tools/tsc_oracle_case.mjs): oracle=7 engine=4 agree=4 extra=0. runDirect, and
# each step's own call to measure, resolve and are the controls.
pipeline#runIterated(Node) -> steps#widenRange(Node)
pipeline#runIndexed(Node) -> steps#widenRange(Node)
pipeline#runByName(Node) -> steps#squareRange(Node)
